        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "Add Cursor and filter widget provider options",
        "body": "## Summary\n\n- Add Cursor to configurable and interactive CodexBar widgets.\n- Filter provider choices to widget-capable providers enabled in CodexBar settings, preserving settings order.\n- Default new widgets to the first enabled supported provider, with a Codex fallback only when WidgetKit needs a valid choice.\n- Keep persisted widget selections stable while preventing disabled providers from rendering retained usage data.\n- Label legacy Cursor request quotas as `Requests`; label current Cursor quota rows as `Total`, `Auto`, and `API`.\n- Add focused regression coverage and document the provider-choice, fallback, and disabled-state contracts.\n\nFixes #2040.\n\n## Foundation\n\nThis keeps the existing widget snapshot and App Intents architecture:\n\n- `ProviderChoice` remains the stable enum persisted by widget configurations.\n- `EnabledProviderOptionsProvider` derives dynamic choices from `WidgetSnapshot.enabledProviders`.\n- Unsupported providers are omitted through the existing `UsageProvider` to `ProviderChoice` mapping.\n- `WidgetSnapshot.enabledEntry(for:)` is the shared eligibility gate for Usage, History, Metric, Switcher, and Burn Down surfaces, so retained entries remain available for re-enabling without leaking stale data while disabled.\n- Before the first snapshot exists, all widget-capable providers remain available; if no enabled provider supports widgets, Codex is the configuration fallback.\n\n## Verification\n\nExact candidate: `b45ccc21e5b3a46889c66c86c2913c9397ea2581`\n\n- `swift test --filter WidgetSnapshotTests` — 21 tests passed across 3 suites.\n- `swift test --filter CodexBarWidgetProviderTests` — 50 tests passed.\n- `make check` — SwiftFormat and SwiftLint clean.\n- `make test` — 601/601 selections passed across 51/51 groups; zero failures, retries, or timeouts.\n- Structured review and source-blind behavior validation — clean/pass.\n- Signed debug app and widget — strict code-sign verification passed; Gatekeeper accepted the Developer ID build.\n- Live macOS 27 beta gallery — exact-head extension rendered Cursor before z.ai and showed `Total`, `Auto`, and `API` in small, medium, and large previews.\n- Live placed-widget checks — small and medium switchers fit both provider chips plus all three quota rows; selection persisted across an exact extension-process restart.\n- Live state checks — an all-disabled snapshot rendered the empty fallback instead of retained Cursor/Codex data; a legacy snapshot rendered `Requests` in every supported preview size.\n\nLive screenshots were retained locally for verification and were not uploaded.\n\nThanks @Zihao-Qi for the contribution.\n",
